title: A font picker
intro: Every font field picks from fonts shown in their own faces: the ones safe to ship first, and fonts only on this PC set apart.
project: Arcade | Font Picker

chapter: Fonts in their own faces | The Font field's list
select: Title
say: A Text's Font field now has a list of fonts, each one shown in its own face.
click: pick:Text.Font
wait: 1
explain: picker:list | Fonts | First the fonts that are safe to ship: the built-in font, the free fonts that come with Griff, and font files in the project. Then, set apart under a warning, fonts only installed on this computer.
explain: picker:Fonts/PressStart2P-Regular.ttf | Free fonts | Griff comes with four free fonts for games, a pixel font, a clean sans, a serif and a mono, all under the SIL Open Font License.
say: Pick the pixel font for the arcade's title.
pick: Text.Font = Fonts/PressStart2P-Regular.ttf
expectvalue: Title.Text.Font = Fonts/PressStart2P-Regular.ttf
expectflagged: Text.Font = none
expectfile: Fonts/PressStart2P-Regular.ttf
expectfile: Fonts/PressStart2P-OFL.txt
explain: scene | Scene view | Picking it copied the font and its license into the project's Assets, so the game ships it, and its third party notices name it.

chapter: Installed fonts | Only on this PC
select: Best
pick: Text.Font = Consolas
expectvalue: Best.Text.Font = Consolas
explain: field:Text.Font | Not shipped | An installed font still draws on your own computer, but it's never copied into the game. Players may not have it, a browser never does, and both exports warn of it.
set: Text.Font = Nofont Sans
expectflagged: Text.Font = Nofont Sans
explain: field:Text.Font | Flagged | A font that's nowhere, no file in Assets and nothing installed, is flagged, as the built-in font would draw instead.

chapter: Free fonts from the menu | Art > Add Free Font
menu: Art > Add Free Font > Crimson Text SemiBold
expectvalue: Best.Text.Font = Fonts/CrimsonText-SemiBold.ttf
expectfile: Fonts/CrimsonText-OFL.txt
expectflagged: Text.Font = none
say: Art, Add Free Font does the same from the menu, and sets the selected text in it. Agents get the same choices through the editor's MCP.

chapter: Every language | What no font of the game's has
set: Text.Value = Best 你好 こんにちは 😀
expectvalue: Best.Text.Value = Best 你好 こんにちは 😀
explain: scene | Scene view | Chinese, Japanese and emoji come from Windows' own fonts again, a letter at a time, on the computer the game runs on. They're never shipped with the game.
